-- title:
--   Closedness of the uniformised locus in the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$, a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring, an irreducible $\pi\in\mathcal O$ with $\mathcal O$ complete for the $\pi$-adic topology, $\#(\mathcal O/\pi)=r$ and $(r)=(\pi)$, and a fraction field $K_0$ of $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero. Let $Onr$ be a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$-algebra with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, with that ideal maximal, such that every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$, and $Fr(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod\pi$. Let $v\!\det:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) be a homomorphism with $v\!\det(g)=n$ exactly when $\det g=u\pi^{n}$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^{\times}$. Let $G$ be a group, $\sigma:G\to\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, $\Gamma\le G$ containing an element $z$ with $\sigma z$ scalar and $v\!\det(\sigma z)=2$ and an element $w$ with $v\!\det(\sigma w)=1$, and let $\Gamma'$ be the subgroup of elements of $\Gamma$ with $v\!\det\circ\sigma$ even. Let $\rho:G\to\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ be induced by $\sigma$, with $\rho(\Gamma')$ acting on the vertices of the lattice tree of $(\mathcal O,K_0)$ with finite vertex stabilisers and with finitely many orbits. Let $f:\mathcal X\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ be proper, and let $\Theta$ assign, to each $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, a map from pairs $(\psi,P)$ with $\psi:Onr\to B$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra map and $P$ a Deligne datum over $B$ (a family of $B$-submodules $\mathrm{line}(M)\subseteq B\otimes_{\mathcal O}M$, indexed by the full lattices $M$ in $K_0^2$, with invertible quotients, compatible with inclusions of lattices and with homotheties, and non-degenerate at every prime of $B$) to the set of morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}B\to\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$; assume $\Theta$ is natural in $B$ along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps, and invariant under the twisted $\Gamma$-action, i.e. $\Theta(x')=\Theta(x)$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma$, $x'$ has first component the $Fr$-twist of that of $x$ by $-v\!\det(\sigma\gamma)$ and second component the pullback of that of $x$ along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$. Let $s_0$ be $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the quotient map $\mathcal O\to\mathcal O/\pi$. Then there is a closed subset $Z$ of the underlying space of the special fibre $\mathcal X\times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O}\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi)$ such that for every algebraically closed $\mathcal O$-algebra field $k$ with $\pi\mapsto 0$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi:Onr\to k$, every $k$-point $y$ of $\mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ and every $y_0:\operatorname{Spec}k\to\mathcal X\times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O}\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi)$ whose composite with the first projection is $y$: there exists a Deligne datum $P$ over $k$ with $\Theta(\psi,P)=y$ if and only if every point of $\operatorname{Spec}k$ is carried into $Z$ by $y_0$.
--
--   This isolates the uniformised locus of a Čerednik–Drinfeld quotient: the set of geometric points of the special fibre of $\mathcal X$ which come from the $p$-adic upper half plane functor twisted by $Onr$, for an arbitrary natural, twisted-$\Gamma$-invariant family $\Theta$ of points, is cut out by a single closed subset $Z$, in particular independently of the coefficient map $\psi:Onr\to k$; no surjectivity or fibre property of $\Theta$ is assumed. It is used in the verification that a quaternionic Shimura curve with fine moduli interpretation satisfies the expected $p$-adic uniformisation statements.
